## Transfection and luciferase reporter gene assay
A total of $5\times10^{5}\mathsf{S}2$ cells (CVCL_Z232, Invitrogen, Cat#R690-07) stably expressing the pMK33-Flagjumu full CDS construct or empty $\mathsf{p M K}33$ vector were plated per well in a 24-well plate and then cotransfected with $200~\mathsf{n g}$ of dmyc promoter firefly luciferase reporter plasmid and $20~\mathsf{n g}$ of Renilla luciferase pRL-TK reporter vector. The cells were harvested after $48\ \mathsf{h r}$ of incubation. Luciferase assays were performed using the Dual-Luciferase Reporter Assay System (Promega), and the normalized luciferase values were calculated as the ratio of the firefly to the Renilla luciferase activities.
Plasmid transfection was performed in at least triplicate, and luciferase activity was measured in duplicate or triplicate.
